`JsonException` is mutable, notably in [AddJsonExceptionInformation(in ReadStack state, in Utf8JsonReader reader, JsonException ex)](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/libraries/System.Text.Json/src/System/Text/Json/ThrowHelper.Serialization.cs#L347) and [AddJsonExceptionInformation(in WriteStack state, JsonException ex)](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/main/src/libraries/System.Text.Json/src/System/Text/Json/ThrowHelper.Serialization.cs#L383). When converters of complex type throws `JsonException` with `Path` property set, the information will be overwritten. It's better to preserve this information by concating existing `Path` data:

```C#
string path = state.JsonPath();
if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(ex.Path))
{
    path = path + ex.Path;
}
ex.Path = path;
```

